{
  "slug": "phorest",
  "name": "Phorest",
  "description": "Phorest salon and spa software: branches, staff and timetables, services and categories, clients with service and product history, appointments, free appointment slots, products and stock, gift vouchers and reviews. Phorest Third Party API with Basic auth; bookings and client creation are included but installed switched off.",
  "region": "intl",
  "category": "scheduling",
  "icon": "phorest",
  "docsUrl": "https://developer.phorest.com/",
  "prerequisites": "API credentials from Phorest: request API access through Phorest support from an e-mail address registered on your business, with your Phorest account number. You receive a username (with a global/ prefix), a password and your business id.",
  "instructions": "## Phorest\nPhorest is salon and spa software (appointments, clients, staff, retail, vouchers). This connector uses the Phorest Third Party API. Every call is scoped to one business (`PHOREST_BUSINESS_ID`), and most to a branch (`branch_id`).\n\n## Setup\n1. API access is granted by Phorest: request it through Phorest support (https://support.phorest.com, \"API access\" ticket) from an e-mail address registered on your business, with your Phorest account number.\n2. Phorest sends a username and password. The username has a `global/` prefix, for example `global/name@example.com`; keep the prefix. Put them into `PHOREST_USERNAME` and `PHOREST_PASSWORD` (HTTP Basic auth).\n3. `PHOREST_BUSINESS_ID` is the business id that comes with the credentials (ask api-requests@phorest.com if it is missing).\n4. `PHOREST_API_URL`: `https://api-gateway-eu.phorest.com` for Europe, `https://api-gateway-us.phorest.com` for the United States, Canada and Australia. A US account on the EU host answers 401.\n\n## Start here\n- `phorest_list_branches` returns the `branchId` of each salon; pass it as `branch_id`.\n- Diary: `phorest_list_appointments` with `from_date`/`to_date` (yyyy-MM-dd, at most one month apart).\n- Client lookup: `phorest_list_clients` by `email`, `phone` or name (`~Jo%` for a prefix), then `phorest_get_client` and the history tools.\n- Free slots: `phorest_check_availability` with `service_selections` (service ids from `phorest_list_services`).\n\n## Pagination\n`page` starts at 0, `size` up to 200 (1000 for staff timetables). Answers carry `page.totalElements` and `page.totalPages`.\n\n## Data and limits\nThe API is live: it reads and changes the real salon data. Phorest does not offer card payments or Phorest Pay through the API, and no webhooks; poll with `updated_from` / `updatedAfter` filters. Date ranges on appointments, breaks and timetables are limited to one month.\n\n## Writes\nCreating clients and bookings and cancelling appointments are included but installed switched off.",
  "requiredEnvVars": [
    "PHOREST_API_URL",
    "PHOREST_BUSINESS_ID",
    "PHOREST_USERNAME",
    "PHOREST_PASSWORD"
  ],
  "envVarMeta": {
    "PHOREST_API_URL": {
      "label": "API server (region)",
      "kind": "address",
      "help": "https://api-gateway-eu.phorest.com for Europe, https://api-gateway-us.phorest.com for the United States, Canada and Australia.",
      "example": "https://api-gateway-eu.phorest.com",
      "link": "https://developer.phorest.com/docs/getting-started",
      "pattern": "^https://(api-gateway-(eu|us)|platform(-us)?)\\.phorest\\.com$",
      "patternMessage": "Use https://api-gateway-eu.phorest.com or https://api-gateway-us.phorest.com, without a path or trailing slash."
    },
    "PHOREST_BUSINESS_ID": {
      "label": "Business id",
      "kind": "setting",
      "help": "The business id Phorest sends with the API credentials. Ask api-requests@phorest.com if you do not have it.",
      "link": "https://developer.phorest.com/docs/getting-started",
      "pattern": "^[A-Za-z0-9_-]+$",
      "patternMessage": "The business id only, without slashes or the URL."
    },
    "PHOREST_USERNAME": {
      "label": "API username",
      "kind": "credential",
      "help": "The API username Phorest issued, including the global/ prefix, e.g. global/name@example.com.",
      "link": "https://developer.phorest.com/docs/getting-started",
      "pattern": "^global/\\S+$",
      "patternMessage": "The username starts with global/ followed by the e-mail address."
    },
    "PHOREST_PASSWORD": {
      "label": "API password",
      "kind": "credential",
      "help": "The password Phorest issued with the API username.",
      "link": "https://developer.phorest.com/docs/getting-started"
    }
  },
  "verifyHints": {
    "401": "Phorest refused the login. Check the username includes the global/ prefix, the password, and that the server matches your region (EU or US/Canada/Australia).",
    "403": "The API user has no access to this business or branch. Check the business id.",
    "404": "Phorest did not find the business or branch. Check the business id, and use a branch_id from phorest_list_branches."
  },
  "probe": {
    "tool": "phorest_list_branches",
    "params": {
      "size": 1
    }
  },
  "connector": {
    "name": "Phorest Third Party API",
    "type": "REST",
    "baseUrl": "{{PHOREST_API_URL}}/third-party-api-server/api/business/{{PHOREST_BUSINESS_ID}}",
    "authType": "BASIC_AUTH",
    "authConfig": {
      "username": "{{PHOREST_USERNAME}}",
      "password": "{{PHOREST_PASSWORD}}"
    },
    "headers": {
      "Accept": "application/json"
    },
    "healthcheckPath": "/branch"
  },
  "tools": [
    {
